Reasonable Steps (slavery_compliance_agent)
Built for the Open Agent Hackathon 2026.

This project includes:
- test/conformance/world-model-runner.ts, copied from the Meterless engines
  repository (github.com/meterless/meterless, engines/world-model/conformance),
  Apache License 2.0. Only the default implementation path was changed.
- src/engines/world-model/, an implementation of the Meterless World Model
  specification (engines/world-model/AGENTS.md, Apache License 2.0).

Reference data:
- data/reference/dol_goods_excerpt.csv: excerpt of the US Department of Labor
  List of Goods Produced by Child Labor or Forced Labor (2024), from dol.gov.
  US Government work, public domain.
- data/reference/sector_risk.csv: sector list based on the Australian Human
  Rights Commission's information for suppliers on modern slavery.
- The Australian Sanctions Consolidated List is downloaded by
  `npm run fetch:data` from dfat.gov.au and is not redistributed here.
- data/reference/sanctions_test_fixture.csv contains synthetic names for
  testing only. It is not sanctions data.

All companies, people, invoices and declarations in data/demo are fictional.
